# The catalog cannot be read from the launch until the `modelsup` line; a turn
# streams and holds; `/model ` opens the inline column over the failure while it
# runs. fx's column lists its models through `ensureModelCache` in every frame
# that draws it (`footerContext`, `app_render_runtime.zig:561-563`), and while
# the turn streams its activity row animates every 50 ms
# (`advanceVisibleAnimation`, `app_worker_runtime.zig:840-875`) -- so the column
# reads again on its first frame past each failure's hold (5 s, then 10 s:
# `failureBackoffMs`, `beginLoad`, `model_cache_runtime.zig:40-54`,
# `:617@481104fd`), and turns into the rows once the catalog is back. Here its
# first frame is past the launch read's 5 s and reads (503), and the catalog
# comes back once the column is on the screen over the failure; `col-held`, 3 s
# on and inside that read's 10 s hold, still says `unable to load models` -- an
# animated frame reads nothing before the hold ends -- and `col-back` waits on
# the screen for the rows the first frame past it reads. The outage ends at a
# line, not at a moment on the gateway's clock, which each binary's launch
# reaches at a different time (registry #19). `modelsdelay 0` stamps each read
# in the gateway log.
models models.json
modelsdown
modelsdelay 0
gateway model-reask-turns.json
wait 4.5
snap start
type say something
key Enter
wait 1
type /model
key Space
until shown unable to load models
wait 0.7
snap col-down
modelsup
wait 3
snap col-held
until shown gpt-6-astra
snap col-back
gwlog
